    <statement><p>The number of bacteria in a refrigerated food product is given by
<m>N(T) = 27 T^2 - 97 T + 51</m>,  <m>3 \lt  T \lt  33</m>
where <m>T</m> is the temperature of the food.</p>
<p>When the food is removed from the refrigerator, the temperature is given by 
<m>T(t) = 4 t + 1.7</m> , where <m>t</m> is the time in hours.</p>
<p>Find the composite function <m>N(T(t))</m>:</p>
<p><m>N(T(t)) =</m>  <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Find the time when the bacteria count reaches 14225</p>
<p>Time Needed =  <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>27\mathopen{}\left(4t+1.7\right)^{2}-97\mathopen{}\left(4t+1.7\right)+51</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5.76966827391021</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
